schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Outdated documentation can cause harm
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Documentation is only valuable if it stays current — outdated
    documentation can actually cause harm because people make decisions based
    on wrong information.
  evidence: >-
    Stated directly in the article's "Maintaining Documentation Over Time"
    section, supported by the article's recommended monthly/quarterly/annual
    review cadence and "Be Current" best practice (date everything, note
    review-by dates, mark or remove inaccurate content).
  interpretation: >-
    Used to argue that documentation is an ongoing maintenance activity, not
    a one-time write-and-forget task — directly motivates the article's
    "Assign Ownership" and "Review on a Schedule" recommendations.
  uncertainty: >-
    General principle asserted from the author's own reasoning, not backed by
    a specific incident, study, or named case in this article.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/documentation-knowledge.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-12f41d6ac647
